  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config_menu": "Config",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.translucency_mode": "Translucency: %s",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.translucency_mode.dither_shader": "Dither (shader)",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.translucency_mode.dither_texture": "Dither (texture)",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.translucency_mode.translucent": "Alpha blend",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.translucency_mode.tooltip": "(Restart required) (Dither (shader) / Dither (texture) / Alpha blend)\nHow see-through vehicle parts are drawn. Only the two non-shader modes work with shader packs.",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.dither_upscale": "Dither Upscale: %sx",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.dither_upscale.tooltip": "(Applies on reload) (0.25 / 0.5 / 1 / 2 / 4 / 8)\nTexture scale before dithering. Above 1 gives a finer pattern for more memory; below 1 shrinks it to save memory on weak hardware. Dither (texture) mode only.",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.dither_max_size": "Dither Max Texture: %s px",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.dither_max_size.tooltip": "(Applies on reload) (512 - 8192 px)\nSize limit for an enlarged texture. Caps the upscale above. Dither (texture) mode only.",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.experimental_triangles": "Experimental Triangle Rendering: %s",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.experimental_triangles.tooltip": "(Restart required) (true / false)\nSubmits 3 vertices per triangle instead of 4. Experimental. Dither (shader) mode only.",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.match_view_distance": "Match View Distance: %s",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.match_view_distance.tooltip": "(Applies immediately) (true / false)\nUse the game's render distance for this mod's entities instead of the shorter entity distance.",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.disable_culling": "Disable Render Culling: %s",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.disable_culling.tooltip": "(Applies immediately) (true / false)\nSkip this renderer's own distance and frustum checks, so vehicles always draw while loaded.",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.third_person_hud": "Third-Person HUD: %s",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.third_person_hud.tooltip": "(Applies immediately) (true / false)\nWhether the vehicle HUD draws in third-person view.",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.camera_distance": "Max Aircraft Camera Distance: %s",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.camera_distance.tooltip": "(Applies immediately) (20 - 160 blocks)\nHow far the third-person camera can zoom out while flying.",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.gpu_compression": "GPU Texture Compression (BC1): %s",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.gpu_compression.tooltip": "(Applies on reload) (true / false)\nStores dithered textures as BC1, using 1/8 the VRAM. Alpha is exact; colour detail is approximated. Goes outside Minecraft's texture API - falls back safely if it fails. Dither (texture) mode only.",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.page": "Page %s / %s",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.server_config_menu": "Server Config",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.server_config_menu.unavailable_tooltip": "Only available while hosting the world (singleplayer, or a LAN game opened to others) - a remote dedicated server's own config isn't directly reachable from here.",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.server_config_menu.no_restart_notice": "Changes here apply immediately, no restart needed",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.server_config.parallel_hit_detection": "Parallel Hit Detection: %s",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.server_config.parallel_hit_detection.tooltip": "(Applies immediately) (true / false)\nBatch this mod's own custom hit detection across every vehicle as one parallel pass per tick, instead of each vehicle checking inline during its own tick. Off by default - turn on for a world with many high-poly vehicles where hit detection is measurably the bottleneck.",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.server_config.parallel_hit_detection_minimum": "Parallel Hit Detection Minimum Vehicles: %s",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.server_config.parallel_hit_detection_minimum.tooltip": "(Applies immediately) (1 - 20)\nHow many vehicles must need a hit-detection check in a given tick before the parallel path above is worth using at all. Only meaningful when Parallel Hit Detection is on.",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.server_config.destroyed_despawn_enabled": "Destroyed Vehicle Despawn: %s",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.server_config.destroyed_despawn_enabled.tooltip": "(Applies immediately) (true / false)\nA destroyed vehicle despawns on its own after the timer below, instead of sitting in the world as wreckage forever. Never affects an intact, still-driveable vehicle.",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.server_config.destroyed_despawn_seconds": "Destroyed Vehicle Despawn Time: %s s",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.server_config.destroyed_despawn_seconds.tooltip": "(Applies immediately) (30 - 1800 seconds)\nHow long a destroyed vehicle sits in the world before despawning. Only meaningful when Destroyed Vehicle Despawn is on.",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.server_config.carrier_runway_width": "Carrier Runway Expected Width: %s",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.server_config.carrier_runway_width.tooltip": "(Applies immediately, new runway tiles only - existing ones keep their own already-fixed size) (10 - 60 blocks)\nExpected runway width, used to size a Carrier runway's own support tiles at the moment mod loading itself happens - before any vehicle file's own actual runway width is even known yet. Set to match your own actual runway width(s) if they differ from the default (30).",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.server_config.projectile_chunk_limit": "Projectile Chunk Load Limit: %s",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.server_config.projectile_chunk_limit.disabled": "Projectile Chunk Load Limit: Disabled",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.server_config.projectile_chunk_limit.tooltip": "(Applies immediately) (Disabled / 50 - 1000)\nCaps the total number of chunks flying projectiles force-load across the whole server at once, so they keep operating until impact even far from any player. When exceeded, the oldest-fired projectile(s) still holding a claim are released first. Disabled (0) means no projectile ever force-loads anything - the same as before this feature existed. Doesn't affect CAS/Carrier aircraft or any other always-loaded feature, which stay tunable via the relevant weapon/vehicle file instead.",
  "key.tudursvehiclemod.search_light_toggle": "Toggle Search Light (Alt: Toggle Nav Lights)",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.search_light_mode": "Search Light: %s",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.search_light_mode.beam": "Beam",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.search_light_mode.dynamic_light": "Dynamic Light (experimental)",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.search_light_mode.tooltip": "(Applies immediately for lighting; the visible shape may need a restart) (Beam / Dynamic Light / Light Shafts / Bands / Dashes)\nBeam: cone, entities only. Dynamic Light: cone, real terrain relighting too (experimental, can affect performance). Light Shafts / Bands / Dashes: alternate beam shapes, same lighting as Beam, that look correct under every Translucency setting. Dashes cuts each Light Shaft into short segments.",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.search_light_brightness": "Search Light Brightness: %sx",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.search_light_brightness.tooltip": "(Applies immediately) (0 - 6)\nMultiplies how brightly a lit search light illuminates blocks and entities. Scales each light's own authored intensity rather than replacing it. 0 turns illumination off, leaving only the visible beam.",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.search_light_chunk_rebuild_interval": "Chunk Rebuild Interval: %s ticks",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.search_light_chunk_rebuild_interval.tooltip": "(Applies immediately) (1 - 40 ticks)\nOnly used when Search Light is set to Dynamic Light. How often terrain relighting is re-requested as a beam moves. Lower is smoother but costs more.",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.search_light_mode.blades": "Light Shafts",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.search_light_mode.bands": "Bands",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.search_light_mode.dashes": "Dashes",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.search_light_ring_count_multiplier": "Ring Count Multiplier: %sx",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.search_light_ring_count_multiplier.tooltip": "(Applies immediately) (no upper limit - edit the config file directly for a value beyond this cycle)\nMultiplies how many rings a Light Shafts/Bands/Dashes beam generates along its own length, on top of its own size-based scaling.",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.search_light_blade_count_multiplier": "Blade Count Multiplier: %sx",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.search_light_blade_count_multiplier.tooltip": "(Applies immediately) (no upper limit - edit the config file directly for a value beyond this cycle)\nMultiplies how many blades a Light Shafts/Dashes beam generates around its own circumference, on top of its own size-based scaling.",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.search_light_block_brightness": "Block Overlay Brightness: %sx",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.search_light_block_brightness.tooltip": "(Applies immediately) (0 - 3)\nHow strongly a search light tints terrain, separately from Search Light Brightness (which drives entity lighting). 0 turns the terrain overlay off while leaving entity lighting alone.",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.search_light_cone_display_distance": "Cone Display Distance: %sx",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.search_light_cone_display_distance.tooltip": "(Applies immediately) (0.1 - 1.0)\nHow far the visible cone/shafts/bands/dashes shape reaches, as a fraction of the light's own full length. Only affects what is DRAWN - illumination and block overlay range are unaffected.",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.search_light_overlay_sample_count": "Overlay Samples: %s",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.search_light_overlay_sample_count.tooltip": "(Applies immediately) (50 - 400)\nHow many samples the search light fires per tick when deciding where terrain is lit - a fixed count, independent of the light's own shape or range. Lower is cheaper; diffusion fills small gaps a sparser sample leaves between adjacent lit surfaces.",
  "key.category.tudursvehiclemod.vehicle": "Tudur's Vehicle Mod",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.search_light_overlay_interval": "Overlay Update Interval: %s ticks",
  "gui.tudursvehiclemod.config.search_light_overlay_interval.tooltip": "(Applies immediately) (1 - 10 ticks)\nHow often the terrain overlay is fully recomputed. This is the search light's own largest source of per-tick allocation, so raising this reduces memory churn proportionally, at the cost of the overlay following a fast-moving beam slightly less closely. Illumination itself always updates every tick regardless.",
